From 93cb369793c043c9db66963f15760e01d09cef55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojyack <mojyack@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:37:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Tegra210: do not apply Cortex-A57 erratum 828024

Erratum 828024's workaround ("TLB maintenance operations might not be
synchronized by DSB instruction", ARM-EPM-049219 v23) sets CPUACTLR_EL1[49]
and [28:25], which disables the A57's write-streaming (no-allocate) mode.
The errata notice scopes the erratum to "multi-cluster systems that utilize
distributed virtual memory (DVM) transactions" - the four T210 A57s are one
cluster, and the A53 cluster is never coherent with them - and it warns that
disabling write streaming "will have an adverse effect on the performance of
memset and memcpy operations".

It does, by a factor of three. Measured on a Nintendo Switch (HAC-001),
upstream Linux 7.3, tinymembench 0.4.9, one binary, DRAM-sized buffers:

                     with 828024   without
  standard memset      3524 MB/s    10666
  standard memcpy      2275          3941
  NEON STP fill        3523         10673
  random read 32 MiB    167.0 ns      166.7

Every full-line store was taking a linefill it did not need: the CPU PMU
counts l2d_cache_refill 1.01 and bus_access 7.83 per 64-byte line written
with the workaround, 0.00 and 3.99 without, and that holds for DC ZVA too,
which reads nothing by definition.

NVIDIA's own shipped R32.7.6 monitor does not apply this workaround on T210
either - disassembling tos-mon-only.img shows its CPUACTLR_EL1 sequences set
only bits 24, 38, 52, 54, 55 and 59, which is exactly what this build now
leaves behind. A soak of streaming stores racing mprotect()/munmap() of the
same pages (83429 rounds x 8 MiB, four threads) reports no mismatches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XS1cX3ePWUM32XJki7eLiV
---
 plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk b/plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk
index 724cfc3..3077159 100644
--- a/plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk
+++ b/plat/nvidia/tegra/soc/t210/platform_t210.mk
@@ -46,8 +46,9 @@ BL31_SOURCES		+=	${TEGRA_GICv2_SOURCES}				\
 A57_DISABLE_NON_TEMPORAL_HINT	:=	1
 ERRATA_A57_826974		:=	1
 ERRATA_A57_826977		:=	1
-ERRATA_A57_828024		:=	1
 ERRATA_A57_833471		:=	1
+# 828024 is deliberately not applied: it disables write streaming.
+ERRATA_A57_828024		:=	0
 
 # Enable workarounds for selected Cortex-A53 erratas.
 A53_DISABLE_NON_TEMPORAL_HINT	:=	1
